  "body": {
    "id": "thm:face-recovery",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "For every \\(P\\in\\mathcal M_{\\mathrm{face}}\\) that also satisfies \\(\\texttt{ass:no-date-one-absorption}\\), the recovery map is well-defined and \\(\\Phi(p)=\\theta\\). In addition, \\(\\alpha_j^d=\\pi_j^d\\), and throughout \\(\\mathcal F(p)\\) the formulas recover the same type masses, the same full component law of \\(Z,X_0,X_1,X_2,X_3\\) in each cohort, the same full conditional type effects \\(\\tau_j=\\nu_j/\\pi_j^1\\), and the same aggregate \\(\\tau\\), up to the declared descending \\(\\rho_j^d\\) order. This corollary requires neither time homogeneity nor a date-\\(4\\) common untreated kernel and remains valid when the common absorbing row violates all-state terminal-rank and positive-transition conditions.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "P",
      "\\mathcal M_{\\mathrm{face}}",
      "\\Phi",
      "p",
      "\\theta",
      "\\mathcal F(p)",
      "\\pi_j^d",
      "j",
      "d",
      "Z",
      "X_t",
      "\\tau_j",
      "\\tau",
      "\\rho_j^d"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:face-model",
