      "thm:active-frontier-recovery"
    ],
    "justification": "This corollary shows exactly what the observable no-date-1-absorption condition buys: active masses become full type masses and at-risk effects become full conditional type effects.",
    "gap": "Existing full-rank reconstruction does not prove this upgrade on a structurally singular common-absorbing terminal factor.",
    "consumer": "Full latent-type conditional effects are justified only when the observed panel verifies absence of absorption at the recovery cut.",
    "proof_tex": "Let \\(P\\in\\mathcal M_{\\mathrm{face}}\\) additionally satisfy \\(\\texttt{ass:no-date-one-absorption}\\).  Because the event \\(\\{X_1=e\\}\\) is observable, every \\(\\widetilde P\\in\\mathcal F(p)\\) also assigns it probability zero in each cohort.  For each \\(d\\) and \\(j\\), nonnegativity gives\n\\[\n 0=P(X_1=e\\mid D=d)=\\sum_{j=1}^2P(Z=j,X_1=e\\mid D=d),\n\\]\nso each summand is zero.  Hence\n\\[\n \\pi_j^d=P(Z=j\\mid D=d)\n =P(Z=j,X_1\\in\\mathcal A\\mid D=d)=\\alpha_j^d.               \\tag{1}\n\\]\nThe broad recovery theorem \\(\\texttt{thm:active-frontier-recovery}\\) identifies the entire component sublaw on \\(\\{X_1\\in\\mathcal A\\}\\); under the present restriction that event has conditional probability one, so this is the full component law of \\((Z,X_0,X_1,X_2,X_3)\\).  In particular,\n\\[\n P(X_2\\in\\cdot\\mid D=d,Z=j)\n =(\\pi_j^d)^{-1}s_j^dQ_j.                                   \\tag{2}\n\\]\nBy the same causal conditioning used in that theorem,\n\\[\n \\tau_j\n =P(X_2\\in\\cdot\\mid D=1,Z=j)(R_j^1-R_j^0)\n =\\frac{\\nu_j}{\\pi_j^1}=\\eta_j.                            \\tag{3}\n\\]\nEquations (1)--(3) recover \\(\\pi_j^d\\), the full conditional component laws, \\(\\tau_j\\), and \\(\\tau=\\sum_j\\pi_j^1\\tau_j=\\sum_j\\nu_j\\), in the common descending signature order, throughout the full compatible fiber.  They also prove \\(\\Phi(p)=\\theta\\) for the contribution-and-aggregate target.  Since the broad theorem did not use date \\(4\\) or time homogeneity, neither does this corollary.  At the absorbing cut the common exit row remains \\((0,0,1)\\), so the all-state terminal factor is singular and strict positivity fails even though the four active minors suffice.",
